#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:302
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Database Server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:308
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad will store all content in a Database. We supported PostgreSQL in "
"version 10 or higher. The installation script tries to detect a "
"MySQL/MariaDB or PostgreSQL server during the installation. In case none is "
"found, PostgreSQL is automatically installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:309
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you use database connection pooling software like PgBouncer, make sure "
"to\n"
"use a pooling mode that is fully compatible with PostgreSQL. Typically this "
"is\n"
"called “session connection pooling”. Transaction-based connection pooling "
"is\n"
"not supported and may lead to errors during database migrations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:319
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are still using MySQL/MariaDB, you should [migrate to "
"PostgreSQL](/en/tutorials/migrate-database). MySQL/MariaDB are **no longer** "
"supported starting with Zammad 7."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:320
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reverse Proxy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:323
#, markdown-text
msgid "The following reverse proxies are supported:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:326
#, markdown-text
msgid "Nginx 1.3+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:326
#, markdown-text
msgid "Apache 2.2+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:330
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The installation script tries to detect a Apache or Nginx during the "
"installation. In case none is found, Nginx is automatically installed.  You "
"can find a basic configuration guide [here](/en/tutorials/webserver-config)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:332
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elasticsearch <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"optional\"/> <Badge "
"type=\"danger\" text=\"highly recommended\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:339
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Elasticsearch is not automatically installed. Because it is crucial for a "
"proper Zammad setup, it is included in the installation instructions "
"above. If you want to connect Zammad to an already existing Elasticsearch "
"instance, make sure to use a supported version and have a look at our "
"[config example](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:341
#, markdown-text
msgid "Supported Elasticsearch versions are ``7.8`` - ``8.x``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details Elasticsearch version history)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/package.md:342
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"| Zammad        | Elasticsearch  |\n"
"| ------------- | :------------- |\n"
"| 5.2+          | >= 7.8, <9     |\n"
"| 5.0-5.1       | >= 7.8, <8     |\n"
"| 4.0-4.1       | >= 6.5, <=7.12 |\n"
